Subject: [PATCH 10638/11362] The orphaned stamp reached a capstone and counted
 as satisfied

The chain filed at 10:38 has completed with a victim. exp6840 was stamped
flagged_adversarial at 09:23Z. At 10:15Z a sibling task's commit added exp6840's
substrate string to DETERMINISTIC_VERIFIER_SUBSTRATES beside its own artifact, so
the live re-check went clean while the stamp stayed, with no cleared-note. At 13:12Z
the v598 independent capstone aggregated seven criteria from exp6840 and none
appear in failed_checks, so all seven counted as satisfied.

CLAUDE.md is explicit that a capstone must skip an artifact carrying
flagged_adversarial, and this artifact still carries it.

The measurement keeps this honest. Of 134 capstone modules, 101 reference
flagged_adversarial; experiment_6847 is one of the 33 that do not, containing the
string zero times. So the discipline is normally implemented and this is a
per-capstone omission at about a quarter of them. Reporting it as "capstones ignore
the fabrication gate" would have been wrong, which is why the base rate was counted
before writing the entry.

Two independent defects, either of which would have prevented this: the stamp should
have been retracted through the cleared-note route rather than orphaned by a
recogniser edit, and this capstone should carry the check its 101 siblings carry.

The cheap check is a lint over python/carnot/*capstone*.py requiring a
flagged_adversarial reference. It would fire on 33 existing modules, so it needs a
decision about grandfathering before it can be trusted -- filed rather than built,
the same standard applied to the other guard widenings tonight.

Not claimed: that exp6840's numbers are wrong. It looks honest on its merits. The
objection is that nothing DECIDED it was eligible; a guard edit made it so and a
capstone without the check consumed it.

